3.4 Extraction and scraping. Extract, scrape, harvest, bulk-export, or
systematically copy questions, answers, or card pairs, whether manually,
programmatically, or through Anki add-ons, APIs, or database access.

3.5 AI and machine processing (strict prohibition). Use the Deck or Content,
in whole or in part, directly or indirectly, for any purpose involving AI
Systems or automated processing outside normal personal study in Anki,
including without limitation:

(a) training, fine-tuning, distillation, reinforcement learning, or evaluation
    of AI Systems;
(b) creating embeddings, vector indexes, datasets, corpora, or training examples;
(c) retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), prompt libraries, or agent memory
    derived from the Content;
(d) automated summarization, paraphrasing, translation, or question generation
    based on the Content;
(e) using AI Systems to reproduce, replace, or compete with the Deck; or
(f) any research, benchmarking, or product development involving the Content
    and AI Systems.

3.6 Removal of notices. Remove or obscure copyright, authorship, publisher,
or license notices.

3.7 Circumvention. Circumvent technical measures or Anki export controls to
obtain Content for prohibited uses.


